    "explanation": "Both parties. This was a pooled (RYDE_POOL) booking, so the correct baseline for the route test is the matched pooled itinerary the platform computed and told the rider about at match time — 19.40 km, carried on the trip record as optimal_distance_km — and not the 15.80 km unattached solo estimate that appears in the complaint as solo_optimal_distance_km. POL-RD-12 carries that second figure for reference only and says a claim measured against it fails on that ground alone; that is why the '28% longer' figure in the complaint is not the number the policy tests.\n\nMeasured the way POL-RD-01 requires — on the trace, not the rounded trip-record copy — the distance driven was 20.18 km (EV-GPS-00113). The excess over the 19.40 km pooled baseline is 0.78 km, or 4.02%. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only if the excess exceeds both 20% of optimal and 0.8 km absolute. 4.02% and 0.78 km fail both gates, so no deviation is established, as the rider's own final submission accepts. The trace is clean (100% coverage, 217 fixes at the nominal 10 s interval, empty gaps, max gap 0.0 s), so the measurement is reliable and requires no independent corroboration; and none of the escalation triggers is present — the trip identifiers match across all three primary artifacts, the started/ended timestamps agree, the trace is unimpaired, no phantom charge line exists, and confidence is above the 0.70 floor.\n\nThe Hougang stop does not change this. It was the co-rider pickup on the pooled itinerary, announced to the rider by the platform at 18:42:04, before the vehicle moved, and POL-RD-12 excludes co-rider collection distance from excess in any event. No traffic advisory exists on the corridor (EV-ADVIS-00113-01 is missing and carries no weight), but no closure was asserted, so POL-RD-03 does not arise. The fare breakdown reconciles: no ERP gantries charged, no airport surcharge, the 3.00 pool discount already subtracted, and no charge line lacking a counterpart — so the one route to relief POL-RD-01 leaves open, a billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4), is not available here. The driver's record shows no repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 471 completed trips), so no POL-RD-06 uplift or conduct referral follows.\n\nAs the rider filed this dispute and the evidence does not support the claim, the outcome is NO_ACTION: the charge of SGD 26.83 stands, fare_breakdown.payment_status and refund_issued_sgd are left as they are, and nothing is refunded or paid to the driver."
  },
