    "explanation": "To the Rider and the Driver: this was a RYDE_POOL trip from Punggol to One Raffles Place on 5 August 2026, charged at SGD 26.83. The dispute is about how far the route strayed from the one the platform quoted.\n\nWhich baseline applies. Because this was a pooled booking, POL-RD-12 fixes the baseline as the matched-itinerary distance the platform computed and quoted when it matched the co-rider — 19.40 km (trip_record.optimal_distance_km). The 15.80 km the rider has used is the solo, unmatched estimate (solo_optimal_distance_km), which the same clause carries 'for reference only'. Measuring a pooled trip against the solo figure is the one thing POL-RD-12 says fails on its own ground, so the '28% longer' figure in the claim comes from the wrong comparator and cannot support a refund. The correct figures, 19.40 km matched against 15.80 km solo, are both on EV-TRIP-00113.\n\nThe threshold test. POL-RD-01 requires the governing distance to be read from the GPS trace, not the rounded trip-record copy. The trace records 20.18 km of travel (EV-GPS-00113) over the 19.40 km matched itinerary — an excess of 0.78 km, or 4.02%. A deviation is established only if the excess exceeds BOTH 20% of optimal AND 0.8 km in absolute terms. It fails both: 4.02% is far below 20%, and 0.78 km is below the 0.8 km gate. No deviation is established, and no MATERIAL deviation is in prospect.\n\nThe Hougang stop. The platform's own notice at 18:42:04, read by the rider at 18:42:31 and sent well before the vehicle moved at 18:47:10, stated: 'Co-rider matched. Your pooled route now includes one pickup at Hougang Central before your drop-off. Estimated 19.4 km, 34 min.' The stop was the matched co-rider pickup inside the itinerary the rider was sold; POL-RD-12 excludes co-rider collection distance before the threshold is applied. The driver's chat reply at 19:03:15 ('pool booking, picking up the other passenger, app route') and the driver's statement say the same thing. The rider's submission that this was the driver's own unannounced diversion is therefore not accepted — the platform disclosed it in writing before the trip began.\n\nThe trace. POL-RD-07: the trace is clean for policy purposes — 217 fixes at the nominal 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s. None of limbs (a)–(c) fires, so no gap concession or independent-corroboration requirement arises and the distance stands on its own. On the rider's point about the missing LTA advisory: its absence is noted, and it is the only artifact below full weight (EV-ADVIS-00113-01, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT). A MISSING artifact carries no fact. No party asserted a road closure, so no exculpatory clause was invoked and there is nothing for the missing advisory to exonerate — POL-RD-03 is not the operative clause here and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged.\n\nMoney. Because no deviation is established, POL-RD-02's recomputation never runs: the 19.40 km recomputed fare of SGD 25.67 and the 1.16 difference the advocates quote are moot, and the de minimis question does not arise. There is no billing-integrity correction either (POL-RD-09(4)) — the fare breakdown carries no ERP gantries, no airport surcharge and no charge line without a counterpart in the trace or trip record. The driver's 90-day profile shows no repeat-deviation pattern (0 deviation flags over 471 completed trips on the fields POL-RD-06 names), so no POL-RD-06(b) uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises; no other referral clause is triggered.\n\nOutcome. The rider's claim is not supported by this trip's evidence on the correct baseline. Under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION means that because the rider filed, the fare stays as charged and no refund issues; the present state stands."
