    }
  ]
}

{"ruling":{"ruling":"NO_ACTION","amount_sgd":null,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.95,"explanation":"Both of you agree on what happened; the argument is about which distance figure the policy measures against. This was a RYDE_POOL booking, so under POL-RD-12 the correct baseline is the matched-itinerary route the platform computed when it matched the co-rider — 19.40 km, on EV-TRIP-00113 and confirmed by the platform's own 18:42:04 message ('Estimated 19.4 km, 34 min'), which the rider read before the trip started. The 15.80 km figure in the rider's claim is the unmatched solo reference, carried on the trip record 'for reference only'; measuring against it is citing the wrong field, which is why the 28% figure does not stand.

POL-RD-01 reads the distance actually driven from the GPS trace, not the rounded trip-record copy. EV-GPS-00113 records 20.18 km against the 19.40 km baseline — an excess of 0.78 km, or 4.02%. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess exceeds BOTH 20% of the baseline AND 0.8 km absolute. 4.02% fails the first and 0.78 km fails the second, so on this trip's own evidence no deviation is established, and POL-RD-01 directs NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised. The Hougang stop the rider objected to is the co-rider pickup on the matched pooled itinerary — the driver's 19:03:15 chat reply and the platform's pre-trip notice both say so — and POL-RD-12 excludes co-rider collection distance from any deviation measure. The rider is right that the driver wrote nothing exculpatory of his own choosing; that is simply because the stop was the itinerary the platform sold.

No separate correction is due. EV-FARE-00113's ERP lines are empty and no airport surcharge applies, so POL-RD-09(4) yields nothing. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (100% coverage, 217 fixes at the 10s interval, empty gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0), so no gap-handling or escalation under POL-RD-07 / POL-RD-10 is engaged. The POL-RD-02 recomputation the rider cites (recomputed fare 25.67 against 26.83 charged) is not reached, because POL-RD-02 only runs once a deviation is established; POL-RD-11 does not apply either, as EV-FARE-00113 shows METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null. POL-RD-06 is not reached (no material deviation, no balanced evidence) and the driver's clean trailing-90-day record is context only under POL-GEN-01. The driver billed 20.2 km against a 20.18 km trace, so there is no shortfall and no POL-RD-04 compensation. No closure was asserted and no advisory exists (EV-ADVIS-00113-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0), so POL-RD-03 does neither side any work. The charge stands: fare_breakdown.payment_status and refund_issued_sgd are left as they are. Confidence rests on the two weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding measurement, EV-GPS-00113 and EV-TRIP-00113."},"discarded_claims":[]}
